  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0042-p00042",
      "source_en": "You and I must never profane that one word; do not forget the oath sworn before God. I want not only your softest tenderness, wrapping my heart forever like the sheath of a banana leaf; I want your love to have the strength of pure steel, to build a wall within this flowing life; Let the autumn wind blow every yellow leaf from the garden; let white ants gnaw through ancient painted walls; Even if one day thunderbolts should overturn the universe, they still could not overturn the freedom within our “wall of love”! Written on August 23, 1925.",
